# Use IronBee DevTools to drive and verify Cureva

**IronBee DevTools** is the verification layer for this workspace. Up to three MCP servers may exist (`ironbee-dt-browser`, `ironbee-dt-node`, `ironbee-dt-backend`) based on extension settings.

Only enabled platform sections below are live. Do not call tools for a platform whose section is still an HTML comment.

## Verify against the running app before finishing

Never rely on reading code alone when the change has runtime effect.

- Implement first, then verify once at the end (not after every edit).
- If verification fails, fix and verify again.
- Skip only for zero runtime effect (rules/docs, CI config, comments-only).

## Prefer Execute for multi-step flows

- Prefer `execute` with batched `await callTool(...)` when more than 2-3 steps.
- Use individual calls only when the next step depends on inspecting a result.
- Scenario tools (`scenario_*`) save and replay reusable flows.

