## Browser platform: only IronBee DevTools

For any browser-related Cureva work you MUST use only IronBee browser tools.
FORBIDDEN: Cursor built-in browser agent/MCP/skill, or any other external browser agent.

### Tools

- Navigation - `navigation_*`
- Content - screenshots, HTML/text, PDF, video (`content_*`)
- Interaction - click, fill, hover, scroll, keyboard, drag, select (`interaction_*`)
- Accessibility - ARIA / AX snapshots; refs drive interaction (`a11y_*`)
- Observability - console, HTTP, vitals (`o11y_*`)
- Stubbing - `stub_*`
- Sync - `sync_*`
- React / Figma / Debug - `react_*`, `figma_*`, `debug_*`

### Verify a UI change

Open the page (`navigation_go-to`) → exercise the change → screenshot and/or ARIA snapshot → check `o11y_get-console-messages`. Prefer one `execute` script for longer flows.

Typical Cureva URLs live under the web app (login, dashboard, schedule, patients, settings, reports, and Phase 2 practitioner shell when present).
